    "explanation": "Both parties read the same timeline; what divides you is whether the two spells inside the pickup geofence may be added together. Rider: the car left the bay at 19:02:50 and came back at 19:03:50, so the longest continuous hold was 170 seconds — 130 seconds short of the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum — and POL-NS-06 should return the SGD 4.00 fee. That reading would be right if the two spells had to stand alone, but POL-NS-06(i) permits them to be summed, and both of its conditions are met. The LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-09107-01 is present and populated, type CLOSURE, active 18:50–19:30 over the whole waiting window, its geometry covering the marked ride-hail bay, and its own description records that the temporary kerb closure required pickup vehicles to circulate before returning to the bay. The driver's furthest point during that single circulation was 179.8 m from the pin, inside the 300 m leash. The runs of 170 s (19:00:00–19:02:50) and 160 s (19:03:50–19:06:30) therefore total 330 seconds, 30 seconds above the 300-second minimum. I therefore reject the rider's central claim that the waits must not count together, and the related claim that the limb (i) premise is unestablished. The driver's own message at 19:04:05 that he was 'back at the marked bay now' does not defeat limb (i): the closure required one circulation and a return to a lawful bay, which is exactly the situation the limb accommodates. On the other side, the rider is right that rider presence is not an element of the shortfall route and that the rider track 519 m from the pin assists nobody — but the shortfall route is not reached, so rider absence decides nothing. All four POL-NS-01 limbs hold: the arrived event at 19:00:20; 35 qualifying fixes inside the 120 m arrival radius; 330 seconds of accumulated dwell; driver-terminated with RIDER_NO_SHOW at 19:06:30 with no boarding event. Nothing in POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces them — the arrival marker was not false (the driver was stationary inside the radius, so POL-NS-05 does not bite), POL-NS-03 does not govern because the driver was inside the radius rather than merely within 400 m of it, and POL-NS-04 fails for want of any rider locating or coordinating message. The fare reconciles: the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee of SGD 4.00 equals the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee of SGD 4.00 and the charged cancellation-fee line is SGD 4.00, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged, and both profiles being at 1 and below threshold the anti-farming check on no_show_terminations_30d does not trip. Outcome: the SGD 4.00 charge stands; under POL-NS-07 the driver is paid 80 percent of it — SGD 3.20 of SGD 4.00 — and under POL-GEN-03 the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd mirroring the compensation figure. No referral fires: POL-NS-05(ii) requires a false arrival marker, which this was not, and no POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is met.",
