    "explanation": "To the rider: I do not accept your central claim that the two waits must be kept separate. POL-NS-06(i) allows separate in-geofence intervals to be summed when a qualifying traffic advisory covers the pickup road and the waiting period and the driver stays within 300 m of the pin. EV-ADVIS-09107-01 is a CLOSURE, active 18:50-19:30, describing a temporary kerb closure that required pickup vehicles to circulate before returning to the marked bay, and it covers the pickup road. The driver's excursion was 60 seconds (19:02:50-19:03:50), with a furthest point of 179.8 m from the pin, inside the 300 m leash. The two runs are 170 s (19:00:00-19:02:50) and 160 s (19:03:50-19:06:30), totalling 330 s, which is 30 s more than the 300 s LARGE_VENUE minimum. The driver's chat messages at 19:02:30 and 19:04:05 match that trace. Your alternative reading - longest continuous run 170 s, a 130 s shortfall, and so a full refund - would be right only if the intervals could not be summed; the policy condition for summing is met. The four POL-NS-01 limbs also hold: the arrived event is at 19:00:20, the GPS trace places the driver inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius from 19:00:00, the accumulated dwell meets the minimum, and the trip was terminated at 19:06:30 with RIDER_NO_SHOW after the dwell elapsed and with no boarding. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate you: there is no rider locating or coordinating message in the chat, and your rider track sits about 519.4 m from the pin. POL-NS-05 does not defeat the fee, because even recomputing from the first qualifying fix the accumulated dwell still meets the minimum. POL-NS-03 does not apply, because the driver was inside the arrival radius. The fare breakdown reconciles: the LARGE_VENUE zone fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) tie, and the cancellation fee is SGD 4.00, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4. To the driver: the fee stands and you are compensated SGD 3.20, being 80% of the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee, with SGD 0.80 retained as the platform service fee. Under POL-GEN-03 the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd at SGD 3.20; that figure is the money the ruling moves, not a refund to the rider. No referral or escalation is produced on this record."
